cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the data it generates, please cite both the software and the paper it accompanies."
title: "nonhermitian-vk: reproducibility code for a biorthogonal, conditioning-corrected Vakhitov-Kolokolov theory"
abstract: >-
  Code and generated data reproducing every numerical table in "The
  Vakhitov-Kolokolov criterion beyond Hermiticity: a biorthogonal,
  conditioning-corrected stability theory for non-Hermitian solitons".
  The package computes stationary solitons of a nonlinear Schrodinger equation
  with local gain and loss, the adjoint kernel of the doubled linearisation, the
  biorthogonal quasi-power Q, its conditioning factor K, and the
  exceptional-point splitting coefficient gamma.
